Proprietary commercial licensing policy — effective 2026-11-25
All rights reserved by the authorized rights holders. Future authorized original research manuscripts, software, algorithm implementations, designs and artwork are not offered under a general open-source or open-content license. Commercial exploitation requires a separate written paid agreement with the authorized rights holder. Existing commercial remuneration policy applies as proposed terms, not an automatic debt. Earlier valid licenses, statutory exceptions and third-party rights remain intact. Abstract mathematical ideas and facts are not made exclusive by this notice.

No new royalty-free license is offered for commercial or noncommercial use of protected original material. Any new license requires a separately negotiated paid agreement, except where existing rights or mandatory law permit use. Previously proposed revenue-share percentages are negotiable, not a cap. Public visibility is not a general license grant.
